    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0514" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg432"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. de Geofroy</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 11, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to the correspondence which has
                    occurred between the French legation and this department relative to the alleged
                    construction, in the ports of the United States, of vessels-of-war intended to
                    cruise against the commerce of France under letters of marque issued by
                    President Juarez, I have the honor to enclose for your information a copy of a
                    letter of the 7th instant, together with its accompaniment, from the War
                    Department.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurances of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. de Geofroy</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




                <xi:include href="d429-a1.xml" xpointer="d429-a1"/>
